40 Lakshnur Era during the Pearlpas Intervention. 1st (Rorus) Regiment is stationed in Rorus. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1754 LE:\r\n— infantry: 61\r\n— cavalry: 9\r\n— archers: 79\r\n— artillery: 3."},{"id":"regiment24-0","name":"1st (Kalaoba) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1666 Lakshnur Era during the Altazyan Conflict. 1st (Kalaoba) Regiment is stationed in Kalaoba. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1754 LE:\r\n— infantry: 374\r\n— cavalry: 152\r\n— artillery: 13\r\n— archers: 223."},{"id":"regiment25-0","name":"1st (Nurkoc) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1596 Lakshnur Era during the Gahourgan Conflict. 1st (Nurkoc) Regiment is stationed in Nurkoc. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1754 LE:\r\n— archers: 18\r\n— cavalry: 19\r\n— artillery: 1\r\n— infantry: 27."},{"id":"regiment25-1","name":"2nd (Kharam) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1591 Lakshnur Era during the Gahourgan Conflict. 2nd (Kharam) Regiment is stationed in Kharam County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1754 LE:\r\n— archers: 26\r\n— cavalry: 6\r\n— infantry: 23."},{"id":"regiment25-2","name":"3rd (Kharam) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1449 Lakshnur Era during the Gorthizan War. 3rd (Kharam) Regiment is stationed in Kharam County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1754 LE:\r\n— infantry: 7\r\n— archers: 4\r\n— cavalry: 3."},{"id":"regiment26-0","name":"1st (Erciyulyurt) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1754 Lakshnur Era during the Ulve-Yarelian War. 1st (Erciyulyurt) Regiment is stationed in Deri Yur. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1754 LE:\r\n— infantry: 754\r\n— artillery: 43\r\n— cavalry: 404\r\n— archers: 703."},{"id":"marker0","name":"Berbot Volcano","legend":"Erupting volcano. Height: 4489 m."},{"id":"marker1","name":"Bayanzayan Hot Springs","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 46°C."},{"id":"marker2","name":"Atester Healing Spring","legend":"This legendary water source is whispered about in ancient tales and believed to possess mystical properties. The spring emanates crystal-clear water, shimmering with an otherworldly iridescence that sparkles even in the dimmest light."},{"id":"marker3","name":"Zelhaz — iron mining town","legend":"Zelhaz is a mining town of 1654 people just nearby the iron mine."},{"id":"marker4","name":"Zaram — gold mining town","legend":"Zaram is a mining town of 281 people just nearby the gold mine."},{"id":"marker5","name":"Skurhargalange — silver mining town","legend":"Skurhargalange is a mining town of 899 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker6","name":"Tsenmonkh — tin mining town","legend":"Tsenmonkh is a mining town of 825 people just nearby the tin mine."},{"id":"marker7","name":"Vr'tarkrelrund — salt mining town","legend":"Vr'tarkrelrund is a mining town of 185 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker8","name":"Gulukkzar — iron mining town","legend":"Gulukkzar is a mining town of 1502 people just nearby the iron mine."},{"id":"marker9","name":"Linlurth — copper mining town","legend":"Linlurth is a mining town of 4771 people just nearby the copper mine."},{"id":"marker10","name":"Saint — salt mining town","legend":"Saint is a mining town of 859 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker11","name":"Atibeyli Bridge","legend":"An old crossing of the Totnesford River, rarely used since banditry infested the area."},{"id":"marker12","name":"The Orange Badger","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious boiled teal with sparkling kumis is served here."},{"id":"marker13","name":"The Bright Horse","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious stewed eggplant with hot tea is served here."},{"id":"marker14","name":"The Great Moose","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious poached buffalo with yellow milk is served here."},{"id":"marker15","name":"Shemmar Waterfall","legend":"The rapids of an exceptionally beautiful waterfall."},{"id":"marker16","name":"Alcuthornala Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Pevagostis Conflict. \r\nDate: February 10, 1750 Lakshnur Era."},{"id":"marker17","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=492501489276\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=492501489276\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker18","name":"Emeverguard Giant","legend":"Legends speak of a hungry Giant who inhabits Emeverguard hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker19","name":"Yelge Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Bozte Church."},{"id":"marker20","name":"Aunser Pinery","legend":"A pinery sacred to local Harynfanthonese Deities."},{"id":"marker21","name":"Therius Palm Grove","legend":"A palm grove sacred to local Eldar (Elfish) Gods."},{"id":"marker22","name":"Matorus Crows","legend":"A gang of forest brigands."},{"id":"marker23","name":"Ormstony Monolith","legend":"An ancient monolith. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">༷༙༪༳༡༣༫༌༰༻༂༱༊༈༳༇༚༯༲༶༦༛༜༘༠༄༚༃༬༘༜༈༱༴༨༯༠༈ༀ༭༅༇༴༿ༀ༦༤༧༕༘༯ༀ༗༽༶༓༻༘༇༿༴༪</div>"},{"id":"marker24","name":"Ruined Castle","legend":"Ruins of an ancient castle. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker25","name":"Algerkhan Library","legend":"A vast collection of knowledge, including many rare and ancient tomes."},{"id":"marker26","name":"Travelling Incomprehensible Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this incomprehensible circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker27","name":"Martens migration","legend":"A huge group of martens are migrating, whether part of their annual routine, or something more extraordinary."},{"id":"marker28","name":"Batan Chasm","legend":"The Batan Chasm. Locals claim that it is totally empty."},{"id":"marker29","name":"Aydilbey Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker30","name":"Dustc Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker31","name":"Pirk Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker32","name":"Interdimensional Rift","legend":"A rumoured interdimensional rift in this area is causing nearby plants to wither and decay."},{"id":"marker33","name":"Disturbed Burial","legend":"A burial site has been disturbed in this area, causing the dead to rise and attack the living."},{"id":"marker34","name":"Mubric Cemetery","legend":"This ethereal necropolis seems suspended between the realms of the living and the dead. Wisps of mist dance around the tombstones, while haunting melodies linger in the air, commemorating the departed."},{"id":"marker35","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/196\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups\"></iframe>"}]
